  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "* “Is it raining?” \n* “Is the field muddy?”\n\nBoth questions are really asking one thing: \"Is it wet outside?\"",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/4535de643488ddadd4b1d61cd80897a4-lesson9-panel1.png",
        "key": "undefined-b0c46cf1-796f-4dde-ac7c-523e5f03c1e0",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "You can combine two features into one new feature. This is called **feature combination**",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/b001377df84c71ddf65b8db7fe64fa17-lesson9-panel2.png",
        "key": "undefined-ad6413e5-1684-4c2f-a081-672fb4e2b842"
      },
      {
        "text": "**Either**: *Yes* if **one** of them is true.\n\n**Both**: *Yes* only if **both** are true.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/c839dc57b8a00b24b6f1b124ad105643-lesson9-panel3.png",
        "key": "undefined-21faeeca-a0aa-4510-8f22-97b6fd06d189",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "text": "One good question can do the work of two and make our decision trees smarter. \n\nNow try it with movie scenes!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/40f21af11ad7e82567ee0d372e8bbf7e-lesson9-panel4.png",
        "key": "undefined-700fc24f-663a-46a8-827c-3549ad286425",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "use_links": "false"
  },
